description:
Simplify the Cards gallery so compositions behave primarily as visual design-system showcases rather than mini application workflows.

Background:
The current gallery contains some functional interactions that can materially change a card's content, structure, or height. While those interactions demonstrate richer behavior, they make the gallery less stable as a visual composition system and can introduce unnecessary layout movement.

Owner direction:

* Keep card interactions simple and lightweight.
* Prefer stable composition geometry.
* Remove interactions that materially change a card's height or restructure its content.
* Preserve basic component-level interaction where it helps demonstrate the design system.

Keep / allow:

* button hover/pressed states;
* working Switch/toggle controls;
* working Tabs;
* working Select/selectbox controls;
* simple focus/active/selected states;
* lightweight input behavior where it does not materially alter card structure or height.

Remove / simplify:

* interactions that expand/collapse sections and change card height;
* add/remove-row behavior;
* workflows that append/remove content;
* multi-step flows inside cards;
* dialog/drawer-like flows embedded solely for gallery demonstration when they change composition geometry;
* submit actions that materially transform the card;
* dynamic content that causes the card to grow/shrink;
* unnecessary simulated application logic.

Primary principle:
Cards may demonstrate simple component interaction, but should remain visually stable before and after interaction.

Relationship to <issue id="2ae06001-6683-47ab-858c-f465c504a423" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-83/curate-cards-gallery-composition-order-and-remove-weaker-cards">PUI-83</issue>:

* <issue id="2ae06001-6683-47ab-858c-f465c504a423" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-83/curate-cards-gallery-composition-order-and-remove-weaker-cards">PUI-83</issue> curates which cards remain in the gallery.
* This ticket simplifies the surviving compositions.
* Do not reintroduce cards removed by <issue id="2ae06001-6683-47ab-858c-f465c504a423" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-83/curate-cards-gallery-composition-order-and-remove-weaker-cards">PUI-83</issue>.
* Apply simplification to the final curated gallery set.

Architecture constraints:

* Preserve Personal UI semantic tokens.
* Preserve Heading / Body / Mono typography roles.
* Preserve shadcn primitives where useful.
* Do not remove basic accessibility behavior.
* Do not remove working component states that are useful to evaluate the design system.
* Do not alter the public component/resource registry merely to simplify gallery-only interactions unless dead composition-only code genuinely warrants cleanup.

Stable geometry:

* Interactions should not materially alter the outer card height.
* Prefer fixed structural regions with state changes inside them rather than DOM growth/shrink.
* Do not fake stability with arbitrary fixed pixel heights where natural layout can remain stable.
* Preserve responsive/container behavior.

Examples:
Allowed:

* toggle on/off;
* select option change;
* switch tab;
* hover/focus button;
* selected/active state.

Not needed:

* "Add item" that inserts a new row;
* accordion expanding extra sections inside showcase cards;
* save/submit flows that replace the card contents;
* dynamically generated lists that change height;
* nested modal/drawer workflows solely for demonstration.

Scope:

* Cards gallery composition interaction logic;
* gallery-only state handlers;
* composition-specific tests/browser expectations;
* dead interaction-only code cleanup if appropriate.

Acceptance:

* Surviving Cards gallery compositions no longer contain unnecessary workflow-like interactions.
* Basic interactive primitives remain functional where useful.
* User interaction does not materially change card height or overall composition geometry.
* No card expands/collapses into a substantially different footprint during normal gallery interaction.
* Responsive layout remains stable.
* Light/dark/theme responsiveness remains intact.
* Keyboard/focus/accessibility behavior remains sound.
* Public/shared component behavior is not weakened merely to simplify gallery examples.
* Any removed composition-only logic is documented.
